   @abstractmethod\n            async def query_vision_api(self, messages: List[Dict], max_tokens: int = 512) -> Dict[str, Any]: ...\n            @abstractmethod\n            def has_image_content(self, messages: List[Dict]) -> bool: ...\n            @abstractmethod\n            def extract_images_and_text(self, messages: List[Dict]) -> tuple[bool, List[Dict], List[Dict]]: ...\n\n        class ToolParserInterface(ABC):\n            @abstractmethod\n            def should_transform_tool_calls(self, vllm_sent: bool) -> bool: ...\n            @abstractmethod\n            def transform_qwen_response(self, response_data: Dict) -> Dict: ...\n\n        class StreamingHandlerInterface(ABC):\n            @abstractmethod\n            def stream_with_tool_transform(self, upstream, model_name: str,\n                                          request_id: Optional[str] = None,\n                                          conversation_id: Optional[str] = None): ...\n        ```\n        - **Importance**: Establishes clear contracts for each service, enabling dependency injection and testability.\n    - **/home/g/dev/local/runpod/proxy/services/context_service.py**:\n        - **Summary**: Implementation of the `ContextManagerInterface`, encapsulating the context management logic (summarization, sliding window, tool response condensation).\n        - **Importance**: Centralizes context handling logic into a dedicated service.\n    - **/home/g/dev/local/runpod/proxy/services/vision_service.py**:\n        - **Summary**: Implementation of the `VisionRouterInterface`, handling image content detection, extraction, and querying the vision API with caching.\n        - **Importance**: Abstracts vision-related logic and state (cache) into a service.\n    - **/home/g/dev/local/runpod/proxy/services/tool_service.py**:\n        - **Summary**: Implementation of the `ToolParserInterface`, responsible for determining if tool calls need transformation and performing Qwen response transformation.\n        - **Importance**: Encapsulates tool parsing and transformation logic.\n    - **/home/g/dev/local/runpod/proxy/services/streaming_service.py**:\n        - **Summary**: Implementation of the `StreamingHandlerInterface`, intended to handle streaming responses with tool call transformation.\n        - **Key Issue**: This service *re-implemented* the core streaming loop logic that already existed in `proxy/streaming.py` rather than delegating to or integrating with the existing `stream_with_tool_transform` function. This was explicitly identified as a DRY violation by the user.\n        - **Importance**: The problematic duplication in this file was a key point of user feedback regarding protocol adherence.\n    - **/home/g/dev/local/runpod/proxy/services/__init__.py**:\n        - **Summary**: Defines the `ServiceManager` class, which acts as a simple dependency injection container, providing singleton instances of each service.\n        - **Code Snippet**:\n        ```python\n        from .context_service import ContextService\n        from .vision_service import VisionService\n        from .tool_service import ToolService\n        from .streaming_service import StreamingService\n\n        class ServiceManager:\n            def __init__(self):\n                self._context_service = None\n                self._vision_service = None\n                self._tool_service = None\n                self._streaming_service = None\n\n            @property\n            def context_service(self):\n                if self._context_service is None:\n                    self._context_service = ContextService()\n                return self._context_service\n\n            @property\n            def vision_service(self):\n                if self._vision_service is None:\n                    self._vision_service = VisionService()\n                return self._vision_service\n\n            @property\n            def tool_service(self):\n                if self._tool_service is None:\n