            "arguments": "{\"path\":\"/home/g/dev/local/runpod/CLIPPY_MKII_IMPROVEMENTS_SUMMARY.md\",\"contents\":\"# Summary of CLIPPY_MKII Protocol Improvements\\n\\nThis document summarizes the key improvements made to the CLIPPY_MKII protocol to better prevent DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself) violations like the one encountered during the implementation of the streaming service.\\n\\n## Key Improvements Made\\n\\n### 1. Enhanced DRY Enforcement in Implementation Phase\\nAdded specific requirements in the A1.2 IMPLEMENT section to:\\n- Explicitly require checking for code duplication before implementing new functionality\\n- Mandate documenting whether logic is being reused or reimplemented\\n- Require justification for any intentional reimplementations\\n\\n### 2. Strengthened C1.6 Code Duplication Checks\\nEnhanced the C1 category checklist to specifically address:\\n- Added a critical note that when creating new functionality, search for existing implementations\\n- Require documentation of reuse decisions in the tracker\\n- If reimplemented, explicitly document the justification for the duplication\\n\\n### 3. Added DRY Enforcement Rule\\nAdded a new rule in the CRITICAL RULES section:\\n- During implementation, explicitly check for code duplication before writing new code\\n- Before implementing any new logic, search for existing implementations\\n- If similar functionality exists, document reuse in IMPLEMENTATION_DETAILS\\n- If reimplementing, document the specific justification for the duplication\\n\\n### 4. Enhanced Verification Process\\nModified the A1.3 VERIFY section to include specific DRY verification:\\n- Explicitly check for code duplication violations (C1.6) during verification\\n- Ensure that any new implementation properly reuses existing patterns\\n- If duplication was identified during implementation, verify that the justification is documented\\n\\n### 5. Improved Design Decision Documentation\\nEnhanced the DESIGN DECISIONS section to require:\\n- Specific documentation of reuse decisions when making design choices\\n- Clear identification of whether new implementations reuse existing code or duplicate it\\n- Explicit justification for any intentional code duplication\\n\\n## Why These Changes Address the Original Issue\\n\\nThe previous implementation of `StreamingService.stream_with_tool_transform` duplicated logic from `proxy/streaming.py` because:\\n1. There was no explicit protocol requirement to search for existing implementations before writing new code\\n2. The reuse decision wasn't properly documented or justified\\n3. The verification process didn't specifically call out DRY violations\\n\\nThese improvements ensure that:\\n- Before implementing any new functionality, the AI will systematically search for existing implementations\\n- Reuse decisions are explicitly documented\\n- Any intentional reimplementations must be justified\\n- The verification process specifically checks for DRY violations\\n\\nThis approach follows the principle that \\\"the protocol should be clear enough to prevent the mistakes that were made\\\" - in this case, making the DRY principle enforcement explicit and mandatory.\"}"
