finement areas if design decisions need more investigation\n   993|   - Present as PLAN, not OPTIONS\n   994|   - ARCHITECTURAL ISSUES exist? \u2192 Note impact, workaround needed? (use \u26a0\ufe0f icon)\n   995|   - DESIGN ISSUES exist? \u2192 MUST propose investigating those areas (use \u26a0\ufe0f icon)\n   996|   - IMPLEMENTATION READINESS = [NOT READY]? \u2192 List what needs investigation (this is expected and normal) and suggest \"c\" to continue (use \u26a0\ufe0f icon)\n   997|   - Design summary: High-level design + implementation details (prose descriptions only, NO code snippets or method signatures, 1-2 line code examples maximum if critical) - shown when investigation scope sufficient\n   998|   - Use \ud83d\udccb icon for design proposals\n   999|   - ONLY USER decides via \"i\" when to begin coding (only available when Implementation Readiness = [READY])\n  1000|5. **Menu** - Format clearly with visual separation\n  1001|   - **Show menu:** After EACH investigation cycle (always available during A1.1), during A1.2, during A1.3\n  1002|   - **Context-driven:** Show ONLY options for current phase (A1.1 shows c/i, A1.2 shows c/v, A1.3 shows c/d)\n  1003|   - **Title:** \"**Menu:**\" (no phase prefix)\n  1004|   - **Note:** \"i\" option should be disabled/not shown if Implementation Readiness = [NOT READY] (show message explaining why)\n  1005|\n  1006|**OUTPUT RULES:**\n  1007|- Tracker = single source of truth - AI collects detailed evidence internally for verification, but shows concise summary to human\n  1008|- Show unified tracker after EACH investigation cycle (with menu)\n  1009|- FINDINGS entries: Summary line (component/instance counts) + concise pattern explanation (detailed evidence collected internally by AI but not displayed)\n  1010|- ARCHITECTURAL ISSUES: Use formatted layout with Impact and Found at on separate indented lines\n  1011|- **DESIGN entries:** Group related decisions when possible for better readability. Summarize references (e.g., \"across 5 components (86 instances)\") rather than listing all component:line numbers unless critical. Use sub-items for key decisions when grouping.\n  1012|- \"Evidence gathered\" = brief summary (1-2 sentences) of new verifications this cycle\n  1013|- \"Next proposal\" references ASSUMPTIONS from tracker (for verification) OR design refinement areas, does not duplicate design\n  1014|- DO NOT show checklist iteration or duplicate tracker content\n  1015|- **Flow:** Investigation cycles continue until user chooses \"i\" to implement - menu always available\n  1016|- **CRITICAL:** AI must still complete all verification steps internally per V1 (document discovery paths, etc.) even though detailed evidence is not shown in output\n  1017|\n  1018|**Menu enforcement (BEFORE showing menu):**\n  1019|- [ ] Am I showing ONLY options for current phase?\n  1020|  - NO \u2192 CANNOT proceed. Show only options for current phase (A1.1: c/i, A1.2: c/v, A1.3: c/d).\n  1021|  - YES \u2192 Evidence: [Menu shows only current phase options]\n  1022|- [ ] Menu title is \"**Menu:**\" (no phase prefix)?\n  1023|  - NO \u2192 CANNOT proceed. Use \"**Menu:**\" as title, not \"During... Menu:\".\n  1024|  - YES \u2192 Evidence: [Title format correct]\n  1025|\n  1026|---\n  1027|\n  1028|## MENU\n  1029|\n  1030|**Menu Display (show after each cycle):**\n  1031|\n  1032|Format menu with clear visual separation and icons. Show ONLY options for current phase:\n  1033|\n  1034|**During A1.1 INVESTIGATE + DESIGN:**\n  1035|```\n  1036|---\n  1037|\n  1038|**Menu:**\n  1039|- \ud83d\udd0d **c** - continue: More investigation/design iteration\n  1040|- \u2705 **k** - check: Targeted C*/P* checklist verification (e.g., \"k C3\" or \"k all\")\n  1041|- \ud83d\ude80 **i** - implement: Start implementation\n  1042|\n  1043|... or anything else?\n  1044|\n  1045|---\n  1046|```\n  1047|\n  1048|**During A1.2 IMPLEMENT:**\n  1049|```\n  1050|---\n  1051|\n  1052|**Menu:**\n  1053|- \u27a1\u