SSUES, update if new evidence contradicts]\n  1098|- [ ] Will I re-evaluate readiness state after updating findings/design/implementation details?\n  1099|  - NO \u2192 CANNOT proceed. Must re-evaluate IMPLEMENTATION READINESS when dependencies change.\n  1100|  - YES \u2192 Evidence: [Will review IMPLEMENTATION DETAILS and re-run PRE-FLIGHT CHECK if needed, update IMPLEMENTATION READINESS status]\n  1101|- [ ] Will I re-verify already [VERIFIED] findings without new evidence?\n  1102|  - YES \u2192 CANNOT proceed. Reuse verified findings from tracker, only investigate NEW areas unless new evidence warrants re-evaluation.\n  1103|  - NO \u2192 Evidence: [Will only investigate NEW areas, reuse verified findings unless new evidence contradicts them]\n  1104|- [ ] Will I imply implementation readiness?\n  1105|  - YES \u2192 CANNOT proceed. \"c\" means continue investigating, not implement.\n  1106|  - NO \u2192 Evidence: [Response proposes investigation, not implementation]\n  1107|\n  1108|**i - implement:**\n  1109|- Available: During A1.1\n  1110|- Invokes: A1.2 IMPLEMENT phase\n  1111|\n  1112|**BEFORE responding to \"i\" command:**\n  1113|- [ ] Mandatory verification checkpoint passed (lines 330-345)?\n  1114|  - NO \u2192 CANNOT proceed. All [RESOLVED] items must pass verification checkpoint before [READY]. Continue with \"c\" to verify.\n  1115|  - YES \u2192 Evidence: [All [RESOLVED] items verified per checkpoint requirements]\n  1116|  \n  1117|- [ ] Implementation Readiness = [READY]?\n  1118|  - NO \u2192 CANNOT proceed. Show blocking items from IMPLEMENTATION DETAILS section, suggest \"c\" to continue investigation.\n  1119|  - YES \u2192 Continue to next check\n  1120|  \n  1121|- [ ] All implementation details are [RESOLVED] OR explicitly deferred with justification?\n  1122|  - NO \u2192 CANNOT proceed. Show [PENDING] items that need resolution, suggest \"c\" to continue investigation.\n  1123|  - YES \u2192 Continue to next check\n  1124|  \n  1125|- [ ] All design decisions are [VERIFIED] OR have explicit \"cannot resolve until implementation\" justification?\n  1126|  - NO \u2192 CANNOT proceed. Show design decisions that need verification, suggest \"c\" to continue investigation.\n  1127|  - YES \u2192 Evidence: [Implementation Readiness = READY, all details resolved]\n  1128|  \n  1129|- [ ] Will I show implementation readiness status in response?\n  1130|  - NO \u2192 CANNOT proceed. Must show Implementation Readiness status before proceeding.\n  1131|  - YES \u2192 Evidence: [Will show Implementation Readiness: [READY] with summary of steps]\n  1132|  \n  1133|**THEN:**\n  1134|- Show Implementation Readiness: [READY]\n  1135|- Show summary of implementation steps from IMPLEMENTATION DETAILS section\n  1136|- Proceed to A1.2 IMPLEMENT phase\n  1137|\n  1138|**v - verify:**\n  1139|- Available: During A1.2\n  1140|- Invokes: A1.3 VERIFY phase\n  1141|\n  1142|**k - check:**\n  1143|- Available: During A1.1 INVESTIGATE + DESIGN and A1.3 VERIFY\n  1144|- Purpose: Explicitly trigger targeted checklist category verification\n  1145|- Usage: User specifies category(ies) to check (e.g., \"k C3\", \"k C1\", \"k C2,C3\", \"k all\")\n  1146|- Behavior:\n  1147|  1. Identify which checklist items in specified category(ies) apply to current scope\n  1148|  2. Perform verification per V1 standard (grep/codebase_search \u2192 read_file)\n  1149|  3. Document findings in tracker with proper status ([VERIFIED], [PARTIALLY VERIFIED], [VIOLATION])\n  1150|  4. Show summary of what was checked and what was found\n  1151|  5. Return to menu for next action\n  1152|- Does NOT re-verify already [VERIFIED] items unless explicitly requested\n  1153|- Results feed into same tracker as other investigation cycles\n  1154|\n  1155|**BEFORE responding to \"k\" command:**\n  1156|- [ ] Did user specify which category(ies) to check?\n  1157|  - NO \u2192 Prompt user: \"Which category to check? (C1, C2, C3, P1, or 'all')\"\n  1158|  - YE