\"Context management: summarization + sliding window + condense large tool responses.\\n     2|\\n     3|Cursor (docs/blog) does two things we align with and one we cannot:\\n     4|- Summarization when context fills: Cursor auto-summarizes and gives the agent chat history\\n     5|  as a file so it can search for lost details. We summarize old messages and keep a sliding\\n     6|  window of recent ones; we do not expose history-as-file (proxy has no client filesystem).\\n     7|- Long tool responses: Cursor writes them to a file and lets the agent Read/tail on demand,\\n     8|  avoiding truncation. We cannot write to the client FS, so we condense to a preview\\n     9|  (TOOL_RESPONSE_MAX_VERBATIM / TOOL_RESPONSE_PREVIEW_CHARS). Optional future: proxy could\\n    10|  store full results by tool_call_id and expose GET /v1/tool-results/{id} for clients that\\n    11|  add a \\\"fetch full result\\\" tool.\\n    12|  Instruction docs (e.g. CLIPPY_MKII.md) and code files  [... omitted end of long line]\n1251:          \"text\": \"Based on my analysis of the proxy code, here's a comprehensive analysis of the compression features and how they relate to each other:\\n\\n## Compression Features and Implementation\\n\\n### 1. **Core Compression Mechanisms**\\n\\nThe proxy implements a sophisticated compression system with several key components:\\n\\n**A. Sliding Window Context Management**\\n- When conversation exceeds configured limits (token or message thresholds), the system maintains a sliding window of recent messages\\n- Old messages are summarized into a single context summary, while recent messages are kept verbatim\\n- Configurable parameters:\\n  - `CONTEXT_WINDOW_SIZE`: Number of recent messages to keep (default: 20)\\n  - `COMPRESSION_THRESHOLD`: Token threshold for triggering summarization (default: 15,000)\\n  - `COMPRESSION_TRIGGER_MESSAGES`: Message count threshold (default: 30)\\n\\n**B. Tool Response Condensation**\\n- Large tool responses (e.g., file contents) are automatically condensed to pre [... omitted end of long line]\n1295:          \"text\": \"Let me explain these three key compression parameters more clearly:\\n\\n## Detailed Explanation of Context Management Parameters\\n\\n### 1. **CONTEXT_WINDOW_SIZE: Number of recent messages to keep (default: 20)**\\n\\nThis parameter controls how many of the most recent messages are preserved in their entirety when compression is active.\\n\\n**How it works:**\\n- When a conversation exceeds the configured limits, the system keeps the most recent `CONTEXT_WINDOW_SIZE` messages exactly as they are\\n- All older messages are either summarized or discarded\\n- For example, with `CONTEXT_WINDOW_SIZE=20`, if your conversation has 50 messages, you'll keep:\\n  - 20 most recent messages (verbatim)\\n  - 30 older messages (summarized or processed)\\n\\n**Purpose:** Ensures that the most recent context remains fully available for the LLM to work with, while reducing the overall token count.\\n\\n### 2. **COMPRESSION_THRESHOLD: Token threshold for triggering summarization (default: 15,000)**\\ [... omitted end of long line]\n\n... [5 lines truncated] ...\n</workspace_result>"
